 of Oct 12, August to September came in under 90% of normal in 35 of the 75 years from 1951 to 2025 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids. In 2025 that pair ran 48% of normal on the middle, and January to February ran 57%. So far in 2026 on the middle, April to May came in at 65% and May to June at 69%. Every grid had its driest year in 1965, with grid 24822 at 62%.</p>"}
